text:
How this book is organised

Reference - every option of the library in tables generated from its schemas, in four parts:

concepts - rendering, data and mapping, aesthetics and legends, scales and coordinates, layering, labels, facets and multiplots, the theme, shared option groups, errors and limits;
charts - every chart kind: its mapping, its options and examples;
builders - graphs, trees and series built into plots;
data functions - levels, graphs and trees, sets and series, fields, and specific cases.

Use cases - one chapter per family of the R Graph Gallery merged with From Data to Viz: distribution, correlation, ranking, part of a whole, evolution, flow, and colours, in the gallery’s order, each family with its variations.
Galleries - figures replicated from other sources: cljplot extras, the lattice book, Vega-Lite and Vega galleries. Figures are reproduced by content (same data, same idea), not pixel by pixel.

Every example taken from an outside source links to it, and every dataset is credited with its source and licence; examples written for this book credit only their data. All code is Clojure written for cljplot2; no code of the original sources is copied. The datasets are in notebooks/data/ (listed in datasets.edn), not in the library.

8.7 Custom grid
:custom-grid replaces the generated layout with a hand-written track grid (see the cljplot2.layout.grid namespace doc): columns and rows of [:fixed px], [:fraction f], [:measured] or [:flexible w] tracks and items placed on them - labels ({:kind :label :text t :role r}, the role required), or whole plots ({:kind :plot :plot p}). Only :labels {:title t} may accompany it; plots in a regular grid are simpler with plot/arrange.

(plot/render-image {:custom-grid {:columns [{:size [:flexible 2]} {:size [:flexible 1]}]
                                  :rows [{:size [:flexible 1]} {:size [:measured]}]
                                  :items [{:id :main :column 0 :row 0
                                           :content {:kind :plot
                                                     :plot {:data mtcars :mapping {:x :wt :y :mpg}
                                                            :charts [(chart/scatter)]}}}
                                          {:id :side :column 1 :row 0
                                           :content {:kind :plot
                                                     :plot {:data mtcars :mapping {:x :mpg}
                                                            :charts [(chart/density)]}}}
                                          {:id :note :column {:from 0 :to 1} :row 1
                                           :content {:kind :label :role :axis-title
                                                     :text "a hand-written grid: 2 : 1 columns, a note row"}}]}
                    :labels {:title "Custom grid"}}
                   {:width 800 :height 400})





