30.6 Beeswarm
Points packed across their band so none overlap (:fit squeezes a swarm that is too wide into its band). A colour mapping makes groups - here each species is alone in its band, so the swarm stays centred - and the box opts out of the colour with :mapping {:color nil}.
Source: R Graph Gallery - Beeswarm (1, 2, 3). Data: Edgar Anderson’s iris measurements, R datasets package iris (Anderson 1935; Fisher 1936); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange [{:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :species}
                 :charts [(chart/beeswarm {:size 6})]
                 :labels {:title "basic" :x "sepal length" :y nil}}
                {:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :species} :flip true
                 :charts [(chart/beeswarm {:size 6})]
                 :labels {:title "vertical (:flip)" :x "sepal length" :y nil}}
                {:data mtcars :mapping {:x :mpg :y :cyl} :scales {:y {:type :categorical}}
                 :charts [(chart/beeswarm {:size 12 :shape \A :color [215 48 39 200]})]
                 :labels {:title "dot style (:shape, :size)" :x "mpg" :y "cylinders"}}
                {:data iris :mapping {:x :petal-length :y :species :color :species}
                 :charts [(chart/box {:outliers false :color [235 235 240] :width 0.6 :mapping {:color nil}})
                          (chart/beeswarm {:size 5})]
                 :labels {:title "coloured, over boxes" :x "petal length" :y nil}}]
               {:columns 2})
 {:width 1000 :height 700})

33.8 Venn diagram and UpSet
The words three French artists use in their songs: a word is in an artist’s set when it appears in their lyrics. data-to-viz: no more than three sets in a Venn diagram, a number in every region - the UpSet plot handles more.

33.8.1 Two and three sets
Two artists (the venn :sets): circle areas and the overlap proportional to the word counts. Three: the classic layout, counts and shares from a label function (:region-labels).
Source: R Graph Gallery - Venn diagram; data-to-viz - Venn diagram (1, 2). Data: Words in the songs of three French artists, data-to-viz example dataset 14_SeveralIndepLists (Yan Holtz); licence: MIT (data_to_viz repository).

(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange
  [{:data words :mapping {:set :artist :item :word}
    :charts [(chart/venn {:sets ["booba" "nekfeu"]})] :labels {:title "two artists"}}
   {:data words :mapping {:set :artist :item :word}
    :charts [(chart/venn {:region-labels #(format "%d\n%.0f%%" (:size %) (* 100.0 (double (:share %))))})]
    :labels {:title "three artists"}}]
  {:columns 2})
 {:width 1000 :height 480})






33.8.2 UpSet plot
Bars of the exact intersections (largest first) over a dot matrix of the sets in each: from cljplot2.data.sets/upset-rows and membership-rows.
Source: R Graph Gallery - Venn diagram (the UpSetR alternative). Data: Words in the songs of three French artists, data-to-viz example dataset 14_SeveralIndepLists (Yan Holtz); licence: MIT (data_to_viz repository).

(plot/render-image
 (let [m {:set :artist :item :word}
       dots (sets/membership-rows words m)]
   (plot/arrange [{:data (sets/upset-rows words m) :mapping {:x :combination :y :size}
                   :scales {:x {:axis false}}
                   :charts [(chart/bar {:value-label true})] :labels {:title "Words shared by the artists" :x nil :y "words"}}
                  {:data dots :mapping {:x :combination :y :set}
                   :theme {:axis {:x {:label-rotation -45}}}
                   :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 12 :color [210 210 210]})
                            (chart/scatter {:data (filter :member dots) :size 12 :color :black})]
                   :labels {:x nil :y nil}}]
                 {:columns 1 :heights [3 2]}))
 {:width 900 :height 650})

36.6 Accessibility

36.6.1 Colour-blind preview
The render option :cvd draws a whole plot as seen with a colour vision deficiency; plot/cvd-image turns an image already rendered. The default palette as most people see it, then with deuteranopia and protanopia (the render option) and tritanopia (plot/cvd-image).
Source: R Graph Gallery - viridis (colour-blind friendly maps). Data: Edgar Anderson’s iris measurements, R datasets package iris (Anderson 1935; Fisher 1936); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(def cvd-example
  {:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :sepal-width :color :species}
   :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 7})]
   :labels {:title "default palette, as most people see it" :x "sepal length" :y "sepal width"}})


(plot/render-image cvd-example {:width 480 :height 340})





(plot/render-image (assoc-in cvd-example [:labels :title] "deuteranopia (:cvd)")
                   {:width 480 :height 340 :cvd :deuteranopia})





(plot/render-image (assoc-in cvd-example [:labels :title] "protanopia (:cvd)")
                   {:width 480 :height 340 :cvd :protanopia})





(plot/cvd-image (plot/render-image (assoc-in cvd-example [:labels :title] "tritanopia (plot/cvd-image)")
                                   {:width 480 :height 340})
                :tritanopia)






36.6.2 Colour caveats
A rainbow gradient has bright bands that look like edges in the data; viridis changes evenly. Red against green separates categories for most readers but not for deuteranopes: the last panel draws the same colours as a deuteranope sees them (mapped through c/cvd-filter).
Source: data-to-viz - pitfalls; R Graph Gallery - viridis (1, 2). Data: Edgar Anderson’s iris measurements, R datasets package iris (Anderson 1935; Fisher 1936); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(let [red-green {"setosa" :red "versicolor" :green "virginica" :blue}
      deutan (c/cvd-filter :deuteranopia)]
  (plot/render-image
   (plot/arrange
    [{:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :sepal-width :color :petal-length}
      :scales {:color {:range :rainbow}}
      :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 7})] :labels {:title "rainbow" :x "sepal length" :y "sepal width"}}
     {:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :sepal-width :color :petal-length}
      :scales {:color {:range :viridis/viridis}}
      :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 7})] :labels {:title "viridis" :x "sepal length" :y "sepal width"}}
     {:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :sepal-width :color :species}
      :scales {:color {:range red-green}}
      :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 7})] :labels {:title "red / green" :x "sepal length" :y "sepal width"}}
     {:data iris :mapping {:x :sepal-length :y :sepal-width :color :species}
      :scales {:color {:range (update-vals red-green deutan)}}
      :charts [(chart/scatter {:size 7})] :labels {:title "red / green with deuteranopia" :x "sepal length" :y "sepal width"}}]
    {:columns 2})
   {:width 900 :height 650}))





